---
import LandingLayout from '../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
---

<LandingLayout title="Dragon R1 - RamBros 3D" description="Dragon R1 - Open source 3D printed RC racing car. 1/12 scale, dual wishbone suspension, open differential, fully 3D printable." docsLink="/home/">

<section class="py-24 px-4">
	<div class="relative z-10 max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
		<img src="/images/image-1.png" alt="Dragon R1" class="w-32 md:w-40 mx-auto mb-8 drop-shadow-lg" />
		<h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-4" style="font-family: 'Belanosima', sans-serif;">Dragon R1</h1>
		<p class="text-xl text-base-content/60 mb-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto">An open source 3D printed RC racing car inspired by concept cars.</p>
		<div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 text-sm text-base-content/50">
			<span class="badge badge-outline">1/12 Scale</span>
			<span class="badge badge-outline">Open Source</span>
			<span class="badge badge-outline">Fully 3D Printed</span>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="py-16 px-4">
	<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
		<div class="text-center mb-16">
			<p class="text-primary font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase text-sm mb-3">What Is It</p>
			<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-6">A Simple, Powerful RC Car</h2>
			<p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto">
				The Dragon R1 is an open source <strong>3D printed RC racing car</strong> designed for maximum 3D printed parts, easy-to-source hardware, and simple assembly. Built with dual wishbone suspension, an open differential, and a low-noise drive system - it's an approachable project for anyone with a 200mm printer.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-16">
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-5 text-center">
				<div class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary mb-1" style="font-family: 'Belanosima', sans-serif;">396mm</div>
				<div class="text-sm text-base-content/60">Length</div>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-5 text-center">
				<div class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary mb-1" style="font-family: 'Belanosima', sans-serif;">164mm</div>
				<div class="text-sm text-base-content/60">Width</div>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-5 text-center">
				<div class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary mb-1" style="font-family: 'Belanosima', sans-serif;">71mm</div>
				<div class="text-sm text-base-content/60">Height</div>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-5 text-center">
				<div class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary mb-1" style="font-family: 'Belanosima', sans-serif;">1/12</div>
				<div class="text-sm text-base-content/60">Scale</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 mb-16">
			<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
				<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"/><line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"/></svg>
				Fully 3D Printed
			</h3>
			<p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
				As we say - <strong>"If it can be 3D printed, it will be 3D printed."</strong> From the body and wheels to the suspension arms and differential, every major component is 3D printed. The only additional parts you need are common 608 skateboard bearings, M3 screws, a few electronics, and some rubber bands.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="py-16 px-4">
	<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
		<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 mb-16">
			<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
				<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"/><path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z"/></svg>
				Open Source
			</h3>
			<p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
				The entire project is open source - all CAD files, STLs, and assembly instructions are freely available. Designed in <strong>Fusion 360</strong>, you can modify, remix, and improve the design however you like.
			</p>
			<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
				<a href="https://www.printables.com/model/240045-dragon-r1-open-source-rc-car" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Download on Printables</a>
				<a href="https://cults3d.com/en/3d-model/game/dragon-r1-open-source-rc-car" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Cults3D</a>
				<a href="https://www.instructables.com/3D-Printed-RC-Car-Open-Source/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Instructables Guide</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="py-16 px-4">
	<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
		<div class="text-center mb-16">
			<p class="text-primary font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase text-sm mb-3">Features</p>
			<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Built for Builders</h2>
			<p class="text-base-content/60 max-w-xl mx-auto">Everything you need in a 3D printed RC car - performance, simplicity, and open source freedom.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><path d="M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5z"/><path d="M2 17l10 5 10-5"/><path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5"/></svg>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Maximum 3D Printed Parts</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm">Body, wheels, suspension, differential - almost everything is printed. Only common hardware needed.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 6v6l4 2"/></svg>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Easy to Source Hardware</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm">Uses 608 skateboard bearings, standard M3 screws, and common RC electronics available everywhere.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Simple Assembly</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm">Divided into 3 main parts - rear chassis, front chassis, and body assembly. Step-by-step instructions included.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Easy Maintenance</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm">A maintenance door on the underside provides easy access to electronics and battery.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"/></svg>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Dual Wishbone Suspension</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm">Front and rear independent suspension using common rubber bands for smooth, responsive handling.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"/><path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z"/></svg>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Open Differential</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm">Power from the motor is distributed to the rear wheels through a 3D printed open differential.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><path d="M5.636 18.364a9 9 0 0 1 0-12.728m12.728 0a9 9 0 0 1 0 12.728m-9.9-2.829a5 5 0 0 1 0-7.07m7.072 0a5 5 0 0 1 0 7.07M13 12a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0z"/></svg>
					<h3 class="font-bold">Low Noise Drive</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm">Uses a Blheli ESC for quiet, smooth operation. No annoying high-pitched motor whine.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-base-200 rounded-xl p-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="20" rx="2.18" ry="2.18"/><line x1="7" y1="2" x2="7" y2="22"/><line x1="17" y1="2" x2="17" y2="22"/><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"/><line x1="2" y1="7" x2="7" y2="7"/><line x1="2" y1="17" x2="7" y2="17"/><line x1="17" y1="7" x2="22" y2="7"/><line x1="17" y1="17" x2="22" y2="17"/></svg>
					<h3 class="font-bold">200mm Printer Friendly</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm">All parts fit on a standard 200mm build plate. No large-format printer required.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="py-16 px-4">
	<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
		<div class="text-center mb-12">
			<p class="text-primary font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase text-sm mb-3">Watch It Run</p>
			<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Build Video</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="aspect-video w-full rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg">
			<iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/FiOJ_alnoYA" title="Dragon R1 Build" frameborder="0" class="w-full h-full" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

</LandingLayout>
